==Old English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|gem-pro|ang}} {{recons|þankijanan|lang=gem-pro}}. Cognate with {{etyl|ofs|-}} {{term|thenka|lang=ofs}}, {{etyl|goh|-}} {{term|thenken|lang=goh}} ({{etyl|de|-}} {{term|denken|lang=de}}), {{etyl|nl|-}} {{term|denken|lang=nl}}, {{etyl|osx|-}} {{term|thenkian|lang=osx}}, {{etyl|non|-}} {{term|þekkja|lang=non}} ({{etyl|gmq-osw|-}} {{term|þækkia|lang=gmq-osw}}), {{etyl|got|-}} {{term|𐌸𐌰𐌲𐌺𐌾𐌰𐌽|sc=Goth|lang=got}}. All from {{etyl|ine-pro|ang}} {{recons|tong-||to think|lang=ine-pro}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈθenʧan/|lang=ang}}

===Verb===
{{ang-verb|type=weak|class=1|head=þenċan}} ('''þenceþ'''/'''þencþ''' ‘he thinks’; '''þōhte''' ‘he thought’; '''ġeþōht''' past participle)

